<%#
  APP-WIDE modal registrations — the engine modal host's second extension point
  (studio-engine 0.65.0). studio/modals/_host renders "modals/host_extras"
  INSIDE its card on every render path through it, guarded by
  lookup_context.exists?, so a card registered here is registered ONCE for every
  layout that mounts the host.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Until 2026-08-28 this app shadowed the engine's host with
  its own copy of the whole partial, and the only app-specific thing that copy
  carried in its shell was the registration below. The block each layout passes to
  the host is per-CALLSITE: it mounted the host from TWO layouts until 2026-09-09
  (layouts/application for the live site, and layouts/modal_preview for the
  admin modal preview seam), so a card registered in a block had to be repeated
  in both, and a card added to only one rendered as an EMPTY card in the other.
  That happened here before, to the age-verify card. The preview layout is gone
  and layouts/application is the only mount left, which is what actually retired
  that failure mode — this file is the guard against the next second mount, not
  a workaround for a second one that exists today. A card that belongs to the APP
  rather than to one page still belongs here.

  WHAT GOES HERE, and what does not. Only a card with no per-callsite locals and
  no per-layout gating: this file is rendered identically by every layout that
  mounts the host and has no access to a block's surrounding conditionals.
  Anything that needs logged_in?, a feature flag, or helper-computed locals stays
  in the layout block that can supply them.

  Each entry is a template x-if keyed on the current modal id. current() is
  guaranteed non-null here — the engine host wraps this whole card in its own
  outer template x-if on current(). Sibling roots inside a template x-if silently
  mount as a no-op, so every registered partial must have exactly ONE root.
%>
<%# Audit C1 — cosign-rejected (tx mismatch). Opened with
    Alpine.store('modals').open('cosign-rejected', {}) from the entry boards when
    confirm_onchain_entry answers code 'tx_rejected'. It belongs HERE rather than in
    a layout block for the reason the header gives — it is the APP's card, not one
    page's. The BOTH-render-paths note this line used to carry named the second
    path as the /admin/modals gallery, which was deleted on 2026-09-09. %>
<template x-if="$store.modals.current().id === 'cosign-rejected'">
  <%= render "modals/cosign_rejected" %>
</template>
